# ── Google Drive backup (optional) ──────────────────────────
# Uploads are always stored locally; if these are set, each upload is also
# backed up to your Google Drive. Leave blank to disable Drive backup.
# 1) Create an OAuth client (type: Web application) in Google Cloud Console,
#    enable the Google Drive API, and add this redirect URI:
#       http://localhost:5001/api/upload/google/callback
# 2) Put the client id/secret below and restart the server.
# 3) Visit http://localhost:5001/api/upload/google/auth , approve access,
#    and copy the GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN it shows back into this file.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# Optional overrides:
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5001/api/upload/google/callback
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=        # target Drive folder id; blank = Drive root
